# t13_rejects.ledc -- THE LINT FINDINGS ARE THE TEST.  ~41 s
# NOT therapeutic.  Feature family: diagnostics and range handling.
#
# THIS FILE IS SUPPOSED TO TRIP THE LINTER.  Every other file in sessions/test/
# lints clean; this one deliberately contains one instance of each range /
# syntax fault the device is expected to DIAGNOSE rather than crash on.  Grade
# it two ways:
#   1. `analyze.py lint --ledc t13_rejects.ledc` must report exactly the
#      findings listed in the README's t13 table -- no more, no fewer.
#   2. play it with the serial monitor attached: the device must emit the
#      matching config_parser warning for each, and STAY UP.  Fault 4 below was
#      an out-of-bounds write of a whole channel struct past audio_channels[]
#      until it was fixed, so "the device stays up" is the real assertion.
# Blocks 1 and 2 are also genuinely measurable; the rest are graded from the log
# plus "the channel does/does not do the thing".
#
# NO TICK PRIMER HERE, unlike every other file in this directory: the primer
# lives on mask 16 and mask 16 is the thing under test in B1.  So the flicker
# ISR tick follows the file's own rates -- 1000 Hz floor after the marker's
# stop, raised to 3500 Hz by the 14 Hz entry at t=1000 and to 10000 Hz by the
# 150 Hz sweep at t=13000.  That matters only for rate-accuracy claims, which
# this file does not make.
#
#
#
# CAPTURE-INTEGRITY CARRIER (audio ch15, 1900 Hz sine, hard LEFT, vol 40, from
# t=700 ms to the end of the file).  This is measurement scaffolding, not
# content.  A recorder can lose a block of frames mid-capture and still write a
# file of exactly the right length -- the missing TIME is simply absent -- and
# the frame-count check is blind to it.  Five such steps were found in one 665 s
# capture (~1 per 2.2 min), and one of them was written up as a firmware defect
# because BOTH optical sensors agreed on it: the whole recording had stepped.
#   python3 tools/avmeasure/captureintegrity.py rec.wav --carrier 1900 --audio-ch 1
# The tool needs a CONTINUOUS SINE: a session cycling square/saw/noise carriers
# gives ~369 us of phase noise against ~1 us for a sine, which inflates its
# self-calibrating threshold into a rubber stamp.  Hard LEFT so the RIGHT capture
# channel stays free of it for envelope and avsync work.  The marker window
# (0..600 ms) is not covered by this carrier; check it separately with
# --carrier 3000.
# CAPTURE-CHANNEL MAP used throughout sessions/test (see README.md):
#   capture ch1,ch2 = device headphone jack L,R   capture ch3 = photocell on
#   lane B's eye (LED3+LED4, mask 12)             capture ch4 = photocell on
#   lane A's eye (LED1+LED2, mask 3).
# --------------------------------------------------------------- sync marker
0     40 50 100 255 255 255 15
A 0   3000 0 70 0 1
600   0 50 0 0 0 0 15
A 600 0 0 0 0 1

# ---- capture-integrity carrier: continuous 1900 Hz sine, ch15, hard LEFT
A 700 1900 -100 40 0 15 0 0

# ---- FAULT 1 : mask 0.  Rejected at PARSE time, so this entry never exists at
#      all -- it is not merely ignored at execute time.  Expect
#      LEDC_LED_MASK_ZERO and a "channel_mask=0 -- skipping" log line.
1000 10 50 100 255 255 255 0 0 0

# ---- B1 / FAULT 2  1..13 s : MASKS ABOVE 15.  Expect LEDC_MASK_HIGH_BITS
#      (info) on both.  This block is a real measurement and it encodes two
#      measured hardware facts:
#        mask 16 = LED5 -> NO light either sensor can see (-78 / -74 dBFS, the
#                  noise floor): probably unpopulated, so expect NO 6 Hz line.
#        mask 32 = LED6 -> IS visible to LANE A's eye (capture ch4) at -41.5
#                  dBFS, ~8 dB below LED1/LED2, despite being addressed by no
#                  shipped session.  Expect a 14 Hz line on capture ch4 only.
1000  6 50 100 255 255 255 16 0 0
1000 14 50 100 255 255 255 32 0 0
# LED5/LED6 are stopped here rather than at the end: the final stop row below
# uses mask 15, and a channel left flickering past the last entry is cancelled
# by the end-of-timeline handler without ever being graded.
13000 0 50 0 0 0 0 48

# ---- B2 / FAULTS 3  13..25 s : LED RANGE REJECTION IS PATH-DEPENDENT.
#      The freq>100 / duty>100 / bright>100 guards live ONLY in the no-sweep
#      path.  So:
#        lane A (no ramp)  -> REJECTED outright: the entry does nothing at all
#                             and the channel keeps doing whatever it was doing
#                             (here: nothing, so lane A stays dark).
#                             Expect LEDC_LED_REJECTED (error).
#        lane B (ramped)   -> takes the sweep path, which validates nothing, and
#                             ACTUALLY FLICKERS at 150 Hz, above the documented
#                             LED_FREQ_MAX_HZ of 100.
#                             Expect LEDC_LED_OUT_OF_RANGE (warning).
#      Measuring both in one block is what makes the asymmetry undeniable.
13000 150  50 100 255 255 255 3  0 0
13000 >150 50 100 255 255 255 12 0 0

# ---- B3 / FAULT 4..7  25..37 s : parser clamps and ramp-target traps.
#      lane A: R = 300 -> clamped to 255 with a log line naming the field.
#      lane B: 40 Hz, which is also the ramp target for B2's lane-B 150 Hz.
25000 10 50 100 300 0 0 3  0 0
25000 40 50 100 255 255 255 12 0 0

#      ch 16 is outside 0..15 -> clamped to channel 0 with a log line.  It
#      therefore plays on channel 0, NOT where the file says.  Before the fix
#      this wrote a whole audio_gen_channel_t past the end of the array.
A 25000 400 0 70 0 16 0 1
#      freqR carrying an interpolation glyph: atof(">250") is 0.0, so the
#      channel collapses to MONO and the binaural detune is silently destroyed.
#      ledc_format.md lists freqR as a prefix-capable cell; it is not.
#      Expect LEDC_FREQR_PREFIX (error) and, acoustically, NO beat: one 500 Hz
#      line in both ears instead of 500/250.
A 25000 500 0 70 0 3 >250 1
#      audio duty 0 is a NO-OP (the setter only writes duty > 0), so the
#      channel keeps its previous duty -- here the 50% default, not 0%.
#      Expect LEDC_AUDIO_DUTY_ZERO (info).
A 25000 600 0 70 10 4 0 1 0 0 0
#      a freq ramp whose next entry leaves freq as `-`.  The target is read from
#      the next entry's struct member with NO present-bit check, so it is still
#      0 from the memset and the carrier ramps TO ZERO instead of holding.
#      Expect LEDC_RAMP_TO_ZERO (error) and, on a spectrogram, a ridge sliding
#      from 700 Hz down toward DC over the 12 s window.
A 25000 >700 0 70 0 5 0 1

# ---- B4 / FAULT 8  37..41 s
#      `-` in the freq column: this is the entry that makes the ramp above go to
#      zero rather than hold.
A 37000 - 0 70 0 5 0 1
#      waveType OMITTED on a channel that is running a SQUARE wave.  An absent
#      trailing column is NOT the same as `-`: the channel is silently reset to
#      wave 0 (sine).  Expect LEDC_WAVE_RESET (warning) and, in the spectrum,
#      the 500 Hz channel's odd-harmonic ladder DISAPPEARING at t=37 s.
A 37000 500 0 70 0 3 0

# ---- end
41000 0 50 0 0 0 0 15
A 41000 1900 -100 0 0 15 0 0            # stop the integrity carrier
A 41000 400 0 0 0 0 0 1
A 41000 500 0 0 0 3 0 0
A 41000 600 0 0 0 4 0 1
A 41000 700 0 0 0 5 0 1
